{"authorityRole":"external_auditor","by":"buger","candidateKey":"","candidateKind":"","changeKey":"pr/10631","createdAt":"2026-10-02T06:00:42Z","decision":"request_changes","decisionDigest":"sha256:88d3a41eac31a86dc743b65ea89e7b3cb5a400449bc456f28281da741c06549f","decisionId":"rdec-90618fee601c43804dfe86ac2f512456","identitySource":"github_login","packageDigest":"sha256:0da7946a30e0bc02be346a2c685f85132ef686f2f66d58f063480005b0dd2075","packageIdentity":"epkg-97fc71696c1c556dc1105624a5130ef91267ec5330aedd31f2eacbd2d3f3aeaf","prNumber":"10631","reason":"Changes needed for the stated goal (our comment on #10601, re-checked on this mirror). The change is behaviour-compatible: heights are identical at base and head in the real qml6 engine. But it does not remove the quadratic walk: QML tracks every property read inside the functions a binding calls, and rowListHeight / dmenuRowListHeight still read displayModel.count and every row, so a 231-row open still takes 232 height passes over 27,027 row visits (KI-MENU-OPEN-QUADRATIC stays open). The new test checks source text and a JavaScript model, not the QML engine, so it passes while the cost is unchanged. Append the rows in one model update, or take the height out of the binding. The rowsLoaded=false serial bump is necessary and correct. Advisory: we cannot approve for the maintainers.","repo":"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy","schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-decision.v1","scope":"change"}
{"authorityRole":"external_auditor","by":"buger","candidateKey":"","candidateKind":"","changeKey":"pr/10631","createdAt":"2026-10-02T10:28:20Z","decision":"request_changes","decisionDigest":"sha256:e113ef27320920706e6ba623f8e2c72fa5c4a40787ab06932fdc2c75d703c03f","decisionId":"rdec-4ffbf9b0f0ffa22a3208079c439ceede","identitySource":"github_login","packageDigest":"sha256:0da7946a30e0bc02be346a2c685f85132ef686f2f66d58f063480005b0dd2075","packageIdentity":"epkg-97fc71696c1c556dc1105624a5130ef91267ec5330aedd31f2eacbd2d3f3aeaf","prNumber":"10631","reason":"Request changes: the change is behaviour-compatible, but it does not remove the quadratic cost of opening a long menu, which is its stated goal (#10601). Measured in Qt 6.11.2, a 231-option select still does 232 height passes over 27,027 rows with or without this PR, because rowListHeight and dmenuRowListHeight still read displayModel.count inside the binding. The new test checks source text and a JavaScript model, not a QML engine, so it passes while the cost is unchanged. Appending the rows in one update, or taking the height out of the binding, would fix it. The layoutSerial bump on the rowsLoaded=false path is necessary and correct.","repo":"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy","schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-decision.v1","scope":"change"}
